\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Prove discrete instances early. A nondiscrete proof may use a homotopy 2-category or a module equipment only after a comparison witness is built for that specific ambient. It specifies retained 1-cells, cell components, composition, transport, and the properties reflected by the comparison. Taking the homotopy category of each proved hom ∞-category retains its objects; it is not quotienting all boundary arrows by components. A bicategorical intermediate is acceptable. There is no general export called \code{hP} and no theorem that all universal properties reflect through an arbitrary truncation. Where no comparison exists, prove the result coherently in the root interface.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Boundary monodromy invalidates the former shortcut.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{The original schedule “every result in hP first, then lift.”}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-fd-0006}; \ref{at-ft-0008} is retired in its unconditional form. Each concrete homotopy-equipment comparison receives a new test ID and explicit scope.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen restriction on the proof route; constructions later as justified.}
}
